  "summary": "Sun Prairie Police Chief Kevin Warych proposed to the city's Public Safety Committee that the department switch its ALPR vendor from Flock to Axon, after Sun Prairie announced it would not renew its Flock contracts. The proposal includes a 14-day data retention trial, a commitment not to share data with federal authorities, and one-year contract terms, but most residents who spoke at the Oct. 7 meeting opposed continuing ALPR use under any vendor.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The City of Sun Prairie announced that it would not be renewing its contract with Flock for the coming year on Sept. 16.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "Warych proposed reducing SPPD's data retention window of license plate captures to a 14-day trial period and promised it will never share data with federal authorities.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "I also believe that just because something has been ruled legal doesn't make it morally correct. It doesn't matter whose logo is on an ALPR pole\u2026 switching lenders is not a fix for the community's concerns",
      "paragraph_idx": 19
    },
    {
      "quote": "Eight individuals registered in opposition to the Axon contact on Oct. 7. Additionally, 20 residents submitted forms in opposition to be read in their absence as well.",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
